  "method_limits": [
    "RTX 4080 SUPER under local WSL, driver 617.42, 32 GiB modified VRAM, 320W ceiling; remote RTX 4090 native Linux, driver 595.99.02, 24 GiB, 550W ceiling.",
    "Identical executable and cuBLAS 12.4.5.8 binary hashes; instruction scores are medians of 15 samples, GEMM scores are medians of 5 groups of 20 launches.",
    "Both GPUs checked 169869312 GEMM outputs plus six seeded numerical cases, with zero mismatches.",
    "This is a hardware/workload benchmark, not an end-to-end YOLO or DINOv3 result. Driver/platform/power conditions differ. Shape-dependent reversals do not establish an additional driver throttle.",
    "No long-duration stability claim. Telemetry windows differ: local telemetry covers GEMM; remote covers instruction and GEMM, so power/temperature peaks are not directly comparable.",
    "RTX5090 measured stock at existing 575W cap, Linux driver 570.211.01, native sm_120 CUDA 12.8.93 and cuBLAS 12.8.4.1. Prior cards used CUDA/cuBLAS 12.4.5.8. Source workload and launch parameters match, but binaries and library version differ.",
    "5090 seeded validator changed only its architecture admission to accept sm_120; numerical logic unchanged. Diff and original-source hashes preserved.",
    "WMMA/PTX instruction probe is the same workload as prior cards; it is not a claim about peak throughput of all Blackwell Tensor Core instructions. Raw NVIDIA RM rate encoding is not interpreted using Ampere/Ada assumptions."
  ],
